WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:15.989
Good morning. Hank. It's Tuesday March 27th. I'm coming to you from NYU medical center where I'll be for at least one more day.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.990
Sarah was like: 'Make sure they know you're sick!'

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.980
I'm sick: that's my IV port but I'm doing okay, and I'm doing a lot better since I watched your video.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.720
Man, did that make my week.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.010
You know, I've said thank you about Thirty-five thousand times in the last few days.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.460
You say thank you every time the woman comes in and gives you a new IV.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.500
You say thank you, when they bring you your food. You say thank you when the Yeti shows up.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.160
I like the Yeti.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.700
You say thank you when the yeti spends 12 hours a day here.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:52.379
You say thank you every minute of every day basically because you're helpless, and you need a lot of help

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:56.879
and you're grateful for that help, but it's a very different thank you when you're saying

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.100
thank you to someone for going way above and beyond the call of duty.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.080
He said duty.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.080
And that's what you guys did.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:04.520
Thank you in particular

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:10.229
but also all of the viewers to send in those pictures of stuff on their head and for me to be able to learn the

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:15.479
exciting spoiler that Ron Weasley is going to die by a suffocation in a plastic bag in The Deathly Hallows.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:23.159
To learn all of the wonderful things that one can put on one's head from an ironing board to a large

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.400
knee-length boot. I don't know what else to say except

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:31.229
Thanks, nerdfighters. You guys are made of awesome. Anyway Hank the word on the street

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:34.700
Is that I should be getting out fairly soon - either tomorrow or Thursday

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.920
provided things continue to move along as they've been moving along.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.360
If you look at it - it's way better.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.900
Hmm look how much, look how much more white there is!

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.620
You're looking up my nose aren't you? You are. Dammit!

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.860
Hopefully, I will see you tomorrow, here...

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:56.879
...but you will see me on Thursday at 88th Street. Thanks again.

